From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: fix two lock leaks in the wifili path

Two spinlocks in nss.c are released wrongly or not at all. Both leave
softirqs disabled on the CPU that took them, so the next acquisition of
the same lock deadlocks the box rather than failing anywhere near the
bug.

ath11k_nss_wifili_link_desc_return() takes spin_lock_bh(&srng->lock) and
releases it with spin_unlock(). Its upstream twin,
ath11k_dp_rx_link_desc_return() in dp_rx.c, is the same function with
the correct spin_unlock_bh(), which is what the pairing should have
been.

ath11k_nss_wds_type_rx() takes spin_lock_bh(&ab->base_lock) and then
returns without releasing it on two early exits, when the netdev has no
wireless_dev or the wireless_dev has no vif. Every other exit in the
same function unlocks; these two were missed. base_lock is the driver's
global peer/AST lock, so leaking it wedges the data path.

Both are pairings rather than behaviour changes: the lock taken decides
the release, and there is only one release that matches.

Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
index 5ef4f59..f101919 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
@@ -129,7 +129,7 @@
 
 exit:
 	ath11k_hal_srng_access_end(ab, srng);
-	spin_unlock(&srng->lock);
+	spin_unlock_bh(&srng->lock);
 }
 
 static void ath11k_nss_get_peer_stats(struct ath11k_base *ab, struct nss_wifili_peer_stats *stats)
@@ -745,11 +745,13 @@
 
 	wdev = dev->ieee80211_ptr;
 	if (!wdev) {
+		spin_unlock_bh(&ab->base_lock);
 		return;
 	}
 
 	vif = wdev_to_ieee80211_vif(wdev);
 	if (!vif) {
+		spin_unlock_bh(&ab->base_lock);
 		return;
 	}
 
